@startuml seq-err-correction
title BankOCR - Bad Checksum: ERR with Correction Attempted

actor "Operator" as op
participant "CLI Entry Point" as ep
participant "Recognition" as rec
participant "Validation" as val
participant "Reporting & Correction" as rep
participant "Scan File" as input
participant "Result File" as output

op -> ep: Start with scan file path and result file path
ep -> rec: Run with input file path
rec -> input: Read entries
input -> rec: 4-line entries
rec -> rec: Convert ASCII patterns to digits
rec --> ep: Entries with 9 digits each

ep -> val: Run with entries
val -> val: Apply checksum to each number
note right of val
  One number fails:
  (1*d1 + ... + 9*d9) mod 11 != 0
end note
val --> ep: Entry marked ERR

ep -> rep: Run with entries and output file path
rep -> rep: Try alternative digit interpretations
alt No alternative passes the checksum
  rep -> rep: Keep ERR status
  rep -> output: Write number with ERR
else Exactly one alternative passes the checksum
  rep -> rep: Replace number, clear flag
  rep -> output: Write corrected number
else More than one alternative passes
  rep -> rep: Mark AMB
  rep -> output: Write number with AMB
end
rep --> ep: Done

@enduml
